Bug 2052415: Count unread mail across every account's inbox for the macOS badge, not just already-loaded folders. r=arschmitz,edicharry

MailNotificationService computes the dock badge total by iterating nsIMsgFolder.descendants over each account's root folder. descendants only returns subfolders that have already been discovered into memory. At startup the subfolders of accounts other than the one currently shown in the folder pane have not been discovered yet, so their inboxes are skipped, and the counts later load from the folder cache without firing a TotalUnreadMessages change notification that would correct the running total. The result is a permanent, deterministic under-count (typically zero when no account's inbox happens to be loaded) for people with more than one account, which on macOS shows up as a missing dock badge even though unread mail is visible in the folder pane.

Fix this at the source in nsMsgDBFolder::GetDescendants by forcing the message store to discover the folder's children before enumerating them. This is protocol-agnostic (it goes through nsIMsgPluggableStore) and runs at most once per folder. Because the under-count is fixed in descendants itself, every caller that walks descendants sees the complete hierarchy, not just the notification service. Panorama keeps the hierarchy in its own folder database, so it is left alone.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310235


